"comment":"Recorded by NativeGpuClockOffsetVectorTests; regenerate with OPENBLADE_REGENERATE_NATIVE_GPU_CLOCK_OFFSET_VECTORS set to this directory. A row drives NvidiaGpuClockOffsetController.Query or Set over a scripted NVML. The driver has a device count, a name and [minimum, maximum, current] core and memory offsets in NVML units (memory doubled). A fault names a call (init, count, handle, name, get or set) and its 1-based occurrence: it returns status, a get reports current instead of the stored value, and a set stores the requested value (store true or absent), nothing (false) or the given number. Every unfaulted call succeeds. Each expect is the result (the capabilities in editable units, null, or the write\u0027s failure and message), the calls in order and the driver\u0027s core and memory offsets afterwards.",
